The act-break round-trip gap is now confirmed by the owner in the running app, and it's worse than cosmetic: ScreenplayFile.open (ScreenplayFile.swift:63) converts FDX to Fountain on read, Serialise.swift:157-161 degrades .actbreak to a centered line, so a save rewrites Final Draft's "New Act" paragraphs as centered text — silent element-type loss in the .fdx bytes, against the project's FDX-fidelity rule. Draft a lock: make the Fountain boundary recognize canonical act cards (Acts.isActCard already exists — the paste route does exactly this) so .actbreak survives open → edit → save in both .fdx and .fountain paths, with round-trip tests from a real Final Draft file containing New Act paragraphs. Custom (non-canonical) card text may keep the documented degradation, but say so in the RFC. Fail-before: parse the probe file, save, re-parse — act break must remain actbreak. Vibe Check first, wait for my yes.